{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech","id":1408190,"title":"Quastions about inhuman Knowledge Traits ( 6+ ) and Hypertech","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-14T11:17:30-07:00","id":1408190,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Quastions about inhuman Knowledge Traits ( 6+ ) and Hypertech","content":"I noticed few problems while reading the rules in M20&amp;V20. How does their devices and knowledge work for others?<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) Can someone explain how knowledge of physics 6+ works? What does a person begin to understand? How is this different from ordinary physics and what can we do with this knowledge?<br /> <br /> 2) Hypertech/Biotech and non-mages. Let's say we have 3 ordinary people, vampire, fairy, ghost, fire spirit and werewolf. These 8 creatures have found the library of technocracy. They read and learned hypertech/biotech.<br /> - Can 3 ordinary (non-technomancer&amp;non-tecnocracy) scientists create nanorobots? Will they be any different from those created by technomancers or technocracy?<br /> - Can a vampire who has learned biotech create a prosthesis and install it on another person?<br /> - Can a werewolf use laser cannons?<br /> - What are the main limitations of those who do not have an &quot;avatar&quot;? What can't they do without an avatar? Will the mechanisms created by them (non-awakened) differ from those created by the magicians?<br /> - What is the difference between &quot;hypertech&quot; created by sorcerersand non-sorcerers who just learned it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 08-14-2020, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:28:20-07:00","id":1408193,"title":"","content":"2) Hypertech/biotech are basically mundane skills that are used to create magickal equipment used for enlightened 'magick'. Someone with these skills could handle a capital D Device (Hypertech talisman, has it's own arete), capital G Gadget (Hypertech charm, also uses it's own arete, but only works once.) , or other special equipment.<br /> I'd say they can, but wouldn't be able to do anything without their own arete score.<br /> <br /> Basic Prosthesis could be made and installed, but they wouldn't be anything special. If you wanted cybernetics, they would have to be made and installed by an awakened mage/enlightened technocrat.<br /> <br /> A werewolf could use a lasercanon Device if they were willing to.<br /> <br /> Those without an awakened avatar really can't do Magick. They are limited to hedge sorcery and mundane sciences.<br /> <br /> That said there's no stopping the storyteller from coming up with their own hedge sorcery rules, or just reskinning an existing one and using hypertech/biotech as the focuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:52:35-07:00","id":1408203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Actual_Table</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408193#post1408193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) <br /> <br /> Those without an awakened avatar really can't do Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But the problem is that this is mundane knowledge of hypertech. This is not magick, this is knowledge. That is why I want to understand what a vampire with knowledge of hypertech can do. The description of the skill says that it allows anyone to make some devices. Can someone with level 6+ hypertech create something? Or do I need to become a magician or sorcerer for this?<br /> <br /> But what stops a fairy or vampire from creating a tech hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:57:06-07:00","id":1408206,"title":"","content":"1) My personal interpretation (there's a thread about 6+ traits in the Mage forums IIRC) is that 6+ ratings are, generally, supernaturally gated. So the benefits of them come from some level of superhuman ability. For Knowledges, it's easier to approach this as a superhuman ability to connect dots than a superhuman ability to know more.<br /> <br /> So, for a normal person, if you hand them all the pieces of a jigsaw puzzle, but don't show them the final picture, they'll eventually solve the puzzle. It's just going to take a lot of trial and error, until they get enough pieces filled in to start making more educated guesses about what the final picture is, and thus how to sort pieces. The higher your rating (for most WoD games this is covered by Enigmas), the more tricks you understand to speed up the process, but you're still following the same essential process even if you can go a lot faster. Once you hit Engimas 6+, your puzzle skills are so good that you're solving the puzzle in your head just by looking at the pieces, so that by the time you've separated out all the edge pieces, you've caught glimpse of enough of the others to know what the final image is by seeing how all the colors and shapes have to eventually interconnect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:53:01-07:00","id":1408245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408203#post1408203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. But the problem is that this is mundane knowledge of hypertech. This is not magick, this is knowledge. That is why I want to understand what a vampire with knowledge of hypertech can do. The description of the skill says that it allows anyone to make some devices. Can someone with level 6+ hypertech create something? Or do I need to become a magician or sorcerer for this?<br /> <br /> But what stops a fairy or vampire from creating a tech hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are buying into the premises of M20, where the rules for Hypertech are directly tied to the capacity to do (True) Magick or the hedge-sorcery-equivalents practiced by &quot;Extraordinary Citizens.&quot; Sci-fi/&quot;super&quot; tech is basically just a different kind of Magick or hedge sorcery.<br /> <br /> If you want to include that in V20, seems there are three main ways to go about it:<br /> <br /> A) anyone who learns Hypertech needs at least one dot in a sorcery-equivalent, some kind of technomancy.<br /> <br /> B) Cut the Mage bits out of the M20 Hypertech rules and edit them as needed.<br /> <br /> C) Build your own rules from the ground up.<br /> <br /> Superhuman Intelligence, etc., simply has nothing to do with this, from a Mage perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T19:13:32-07:00","id":1408302,"title":"","content":"Hypertech allows both mages and non-mages to understand Devices and other trinkets of technomagick. This doesn't traduce to a capability to create them (albeit those who do create them likely should have a few dots here), but MAY allow non-mages to operate some. And, as stated in M20, may allow mages to understand, and even *use*, technomagick of rival sects that employ a different technomantical Focus (but I don't think this equals being able to *use* said Focus for other purpose than activating Wonders)<br /> <br /> Let's talk a little about Wonders and Focus: Boiled down, Wonders are magical items created by mages, <u>and to use a Wonder you don't always need Arete</u>. Talismans and Charms can be activated and used by normal people (hence by everyone). You don't need to be a Mage to use them because these objects have their *own* magick. However, you need to believe in the Paradigm (Focus in M20) that created the magical item to be able to use them. Also it requires knowing how to use them<br /> <br /> In the technomancer arsenal, both Devices and Gadgets can be used by people who lack Arete. My understanding about how Hipertech enters the scene it's that the skill allows to bypass to some extent the limitation of having to share the Focus. Technocrats don't have the *same* Focus of an Etherite, but technomagick shares enough similarities that a Ctitizen that has Hipertech 3 could be able to *get* what the weird contraption does and try to use it. Also, some Devices and Gadges could/should require Hipertech to operate in the first place regardless of personal belief (you need to know how to use them).<br /> <br /> So, a vampire master of Hypertech can:<br /> <br /> A) Understand what a Technomancer or a technomantic Wonder does/it's doing. Where others see a mysterious glowing ball being manipulated by a crazed weirdo, you know pretty much what's happening<br /> <br /> B) Use Devices and Gadgets of all stripes<br /> <br /> C) Be invited at Etherite parties as someone that actually *understands* what they're talking about (well, as much as it's possible)<br /> <br /> You can't *create* Wonders with mere Knowledge.<br /> But for someone who plans to be *seriously* invested in the world of technomagick, it may be worth the dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-14-2020, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T03:25:16-07:00","id":1408326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408302#post1408302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hypertech allows both mages and non-mages to understand Devices and other trinkets of technomagick. This doesn't traduce to a capability to create them (albeit those who do create them likely should have a few dots here), but MAY allow non-mages to operate some....<br /> <br /> ...You can't *create* Wonders with mere Knowledge.<br /> But for someone who plans to be *seriously* invested in the world of technomagick, it may be worth the dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>...But the skill itself allows non mages to &quot;make some Devices&quot; as per the skill description. While mage books contradicting themselves is nothing new, I think the point of hypertech is to be the &quot;Tech&quot; equivalent of sorcery.<br /> <br /> You also don't really need to stress too much about the arete score thing though. Advanced tech IRL requires very specific tools to create and one of the rotes that can be put on a wonder is the creation of wonders, which is &quot;Cannonically&quot;(as far as any given &quot;cannon&quot; goes in oWOD) create their Device factories.<br /> <br /> You could just just give the hypertech a (secretly awakened)tool requirement, have a public branch of the syndicate sell that tool, and you're done. This would already mirrored to the real world considering custom computer-ware, bio-chemical, and even to-order DNA are already available public resources. Honestly, most people IRL are only stopped from making their own cyber-punk-esc utilities by their own lack of knowledge on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T04:51:34-07:00","id":1408335,"title":"","content":"Hypertech doesn't let you create Wonders without being at least a Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Hypertech lets you build the shell of a Wonder, but without magic, it doesn't work even though it's constructed using the same principles. So non-mage Technocrats and Etherite lab assistants take Hypertech to make parts and items for mages to turn into proper Wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T06:16:09-07:00","id":1408342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408335#post1408335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hypertech doesn't let you create Wonders without being at least a Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Hypertech lets you build the shell of a Wonder, but without magic, it doesn't work even though it's constructed using the same principles. So non-mage Technocrats and Etherite lab assistants take Hypertech to make parts and items for mages to turn into proper Wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>..But you don't need the mage for that even if you enforce a True Magick requirement on hypertech. You can use a specialized wonder to substitute the mage if one is required, and that's more thematic with the technocracy's end goals anyway.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way: Wrenches are a common everyday tools that require complex machines to shape the metal required for their component parts. If you instead think of a &quot;wrench&quot; as a wonder created with the prime 4 effect &quot;Create Wonder&quot;, created via another wonder, then non awakened being able to make machines with it makes sense. The non-awakened simply have the knowledge required to go through the motions of the rituals &quot;Create Device&quot; or &quot;Repair Device&quot; while the wonder does all the heavy lifting.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, a non-awakened wouldn't need a mage to make hyper-tech if the have the necessary tools to do the heavy lifting. It may be that they need a graviton field generator or flux impermeable metals or what-have-you(that they need to buy from a syndicate front company), but needing mages present to do the work isn't required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T14:17:27-07:00","id":1408408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408342#post1408342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use a specialized wonder to substitute the mage if one is required, and that's more thematic with the technocracy's end goals anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use a specialized Wonder that's capable of allow a non-awakened Hypertech knowing character to build the components of a device and enchant a specific effect on them... as long as someone is supplying this setup with a steady access to Quintessence/Tass.<br /> <br /> So, yes, an unenlightened gunsmith on an VE cruiser can have a specialized workshop powered directly by the ship's drive to make and customize plasma rifles for the space marines rather than having one of the VE's enlightened operatives do it. It's very far removed from just having Hypertech and building magical items.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wrenches are a common everyday tools that require complex machines to shape the metal required for their component parts. </div> </div> </div>This is... a very bad analogy. We use complex machines to mass produce wrenches, not because you need them to make wrenches at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you instead think of a &quot;wrench&quot; as a wonder created with the prime 4 effect &quot;Create Wonder&quot;,... </div> </div> </div>Create Wonder can't enchant a spell you can't cast. A Wonder that just has Create Wonder built into it is useless for unawakened characters since they can't cast spells to encode with it. At a minimum, as described above, you need to add at least one spell into Wonder as well for this to work just to make Wonders that do that one thing... and it's all a very Quintessence heavy process which is hard to manage without having someone with Prime around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T01:29:09-07:00","id":1408464,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine the Hypertech knowledges are like having 'rituals' in WTA<br /> <br /> <br /> A Caveat for vampires being that they must have an equal or higher level of (sorcery) comparable to a mage's sphere ratings to be able to work with Hypertech knowledges. (They may brush it off as their own bodies interference with the delicate procedures needed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T07:06:59-07:00","id":1408493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408408#post1408408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is... a very bad analogy. We use complex machines to mass produce wrenches, not because you need them to make wrenches at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, in mage's setting at least, All technology is true magic modifies to work for the masses. So to make the first wrench required a mage who then taught other mages and to let others make wrenches, the guys created wonders that were also wonders imbued with the spells necessary to make a Wrench.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408408#post1408408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Create Wonder can't enchant a spell you can't cast. A Wonder that just has Create Wonder built into it is useless for unawakened characters since they can't cast spells to encode with it. At a minimum, as described above, you need to add at least one spell into Wonder as well for this to work just to make Wonders that do that one thing... and it's all a very Quintessence heavy process which is hard to manage without having someone with Prime around.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can though. Wonders can be pre-built with their own Arete score, then used to created a limited number of wonders depending on what spheres and effects are put on the wonder.<br /> <br /> Besides, if that wasn't possible then the technocracies factories wouldn't make sense(as they break the requirement of permanent willpower for most wonders) and a fundamental aspect of the mage setting would be impossible(technology working at all). There are no other mechanics given for a true magic effect becoming mundane besides reality zones and those don't actually change how reality functions(they change what true magic is paradoxed).<br /> <br /> Quintessence isn't necessarily an issue when you consider sphere&gt;Prime conversions. The wrench in this case would be imbued with a Forces&gt;Prime effect, which would convert the rotational force applied in using the wrench into the quintessence needed to build or repair the wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T08:26:00-07:00","id":1408497,"title":"","content":"I've never seen the idea of 'Mages made all the technology' as anything more than the mages being dick heads who'd claim wheels turn because they made it so. Hypertech is either just outside of the laws of current tech or mundane physics, and the mages are stretching things with magic to get it to work.<br /> <br /> Honestly I get confused with all the Device/Gadget/Whatever terminology.<br /> As the OP said: how would each splat use various grades of hypertech?<br /> <br /> <br /> Like... The technocracy has... what do they call it... enlightened personel? Technocratic hedge wizards? Everyone else can be technocratic hedge wizards yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-16-2020, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T13:41:57-07:00","id":1408568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408464#post1408464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine the Hypertech knowledges are like having 'rituals' in WTA</div> </div> </div> </div>Except not, because it's not part of a ritual magic system where you can use it to learn new powers you don't have. It has some similarities in that you don't need to be a Garou/Fera to learn it, but that doesn't do you much good since Rites don't do anything for you if you're just a normal person (or a vampire, etc.).<br /> <br /> Hypertech is more like Occult: you know a lot about a niche subject that most people don't. If you're also a supernatural of the right persuasion, Occult might be useful for you beyond knowing about supernatural stuff, but not every supernatural is going to have powers that use Occult in their rolls. Characters with Hypertech know about advanced-beyond-modern-capabilities technology capable with magic, and how to identify the underlying principles being such tech (so high Hypertech characters can use stuff outside their normal world view because they can figure out the technological logic behind it even if it uses different principles; assuming they can use the tech with the powers they have), technomages can use Hypertech to great effect as per the Mage magic rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Caveat for vampires being that they must have an equal or higher level of (sorcery) comparable to a mage's sphere ratings to be able to work with Hypertech knowledges. (They may brush it off as their own bodies interference with the delicate procedures needed) </div> </div> </div>This makes no sense with how Hypertech is presented. You don't need Sphere ratings have dots in Hypertech. The only time your specific Hypertech dot rating matters this way is for Mages that have Hypertech as one of their Instruments and you apply an optional rule that when you link Instruments to an Ability, you can't cast Sphere magic higher than your rating in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408497#post1408497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen the idea of 'Mages made all the technology' as anything more than the mages being dick heads who'd claim wheels turn because they made it so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly correct<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly I get confused with all the Device/Gadget/Whatever terminology. </div> </div> </div>There are break downs everywhere. Wonders is the general Mage term for &quot;magical item,&quot; everything else is just a sub-category within. What's important to this discussion are the distinctions for technomagic (only because we're talking Hypertech), and for magical items that can be used without being a mage (because most Wonders require a mage to use, but sometimes they make stuff for non-mages to use and that's an important distinction and relevant to non-mages using Hypertech stuff).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As the OP said: how would each splat use various grades of hypertech? </div> </div> </div>There aren't &quot;grades&quot; of Hypertech. There's just how well you understand how to apply the principles of technology beyond the limits of the prime Reality Consensus. By itself, that's all Hypertech dots represent: knowing the theories about how a class of things work.<br /> <br /> How well non-mages can use Hypertech based Wonders is designated by how that Wonder is created. If it's made properly, anyone (even people with Hypertech 0!) can use it assuming they can use the mundane equivalent (a Hypertech based computer still operates like a computer and thus you can use Computers to operate it even if you have no idea how it works inside the box). These are binary states: either it's made for non-mages to be capable of using or it isn't, and either it's made to be used without Hypertech understanding or it isn't (lots of technomages don't want just anyone using their fancy gear after all). Hypertech dots are just how well you can figure out how things work if you need to understand how things work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like... The technocracy has... what do they call it... enlightened personel? Technocratic hedge wizards? Everyone else can be technocratic hedge wizards yes? </div> </div> </div>M20 hasn't really touched on Sorcerers as part of mage society much. But yes, the Technocrats have operatives that are not Enlightened, but have abilities beyond normal Sleepers. Theoretically RDs could be taught to be such (though the Union is likely to get very shooty if they find out about this). You're more likely to see this from the Tradition's technomages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408493#post1408493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, in mage's setting at least, All technology is true magic modifies to work for the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>False. Technology is a root to bring magic to the masses. Technology, however, vastly predates this process. While mages can argue about the exact parameters, humans are completely capable of bringing about technology on their own (as are more than a few non-human animals). Ultimately there are still the Earthly Foundations, and anyone that tries to build tech that is based in those principles will find that it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So to make the first wrench required a mage who then taught other mages and to let others make wrenches... </div> </div> </div>Again, no. At best the first tools were created when there was no division between mage and sleeper, and everyone could enact their will through understanding, but that's a in-game mystic theory, not a fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can though. Wonders can be pre-built with their own Arete score, then used to created a limited number of wonders depending on what spheres and effects are put on the wonder. </div> </div> </div>Did you actually read my full post? Which included, in the part you quoted, that you'd have to enchant a Wonder with both Create Wonder and a specific spell to be able to grant a non-mage the power to make a Wonder with actual abilities?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quintessence isn't necessarily an issue when you consider sphere&gt;Prime conversions. The wrench in this case would be imbued with a Forces&gt;Prime effect, which would convert the rotational force applied in using the wrench into the quintessence needed to build or repair the wonder. </div> </div> </div>Considering (1) how much Quintessence Wonder creation uses up and (2) how little Pattern draining for Quint nets you, the point still stands that outside of high end technomagic facilities, this just doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T13:57:52-07:00","id":1408574,"title":"","content":"I see<br /> further questions:<br /> <br /> So Glass walkers kinda-maybe have their own hypertech in the form of techno fetishes. Does that count as hypertech?<br /> <br /> Could a vampire not create Hypertech devices with thaumaturgy and a techno-centric paradigm? They too can create fetishes at least. There aren't presently mechanics for this but the magical theory suggests it could be done. <br /> <br /> Do technocratic sorcerers get numina/can they get numina..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:41:22-07:00","id":1408579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408574#post1408574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that count as hypertech?<br /> <br /> Could a vampire not create Hypertech devices with thaumaturgy and a techno-centric paradigm? They too can create fetishes at least. There aren't presently mechanics for this but the magical theory suggests it could be done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) NO! IT is NOT a hypertech. Fetish is fetish. Understanding how to make working nanomachines and clone a cow with them is closer to hypertechnology. Using etheric laser technology is hypertech. The use of portable grenades charged with particles of prime energy making a hole in the matter of the universe is hypertechnology.<br /> 2) 50/50 The Tremere have already created this. The problem is that this is not what you described. They created a new branch of knowledge for the Hermetics. They use their knowledge of Hermetic to control technology and other machines. Tremers can use knowledge of computer, not the occult, in such &quot;technological&quot; rituals. It makes sense - they use thaumaturgy. They're just trying to better write their magic with machine codes.<br /> According to this logic, any Tremer who knows &quot;hypertechnology&quot; can use this knowledge for their magic. But it won't be hypertech. They will simply learn to use the new knowledge for their magic.<br /> 3) They can create fetish.<br /> 4) Numina is non-human powers (ghouls... kinfolks... kinein?). This is almost impossible for a technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:48:59-07:00","id":1408584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408574#post1408574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Glass walkers kinda-maybe have their own hypertech in the form of techno fetishes. Does that count as hypertech?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would count as something you could roll Hypertech to understand how it works, and possibly reverse engineer if creating Fetishes is something your character can/would do.<br /> <br /> Again, Hypertech isn't a power, it's a form of understanding. If a Glass Walker learns Hypertech somehow, they could likewise study technomage created Fetishes for ideas for their own Fetishes (though Garou have easier ways to study these things).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could a vampire not create Hypertech devices with thaumaturgy and a techno-centric paradigm? They too can create fetishes at least. There aren't presently mechanics for this but the magical theory suggests it could be done. </div> </div> </div>Same deal: they can make items that would you can roll Hypertech to understand the principles behind... because that's the main thing Hypertech does when you're not a mage doing Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do technocratic sorcerers get numina/can they get numina.. </div> </div> </div>Depends on edition for how they choose to model this (M20 prefers the &quot;give them some rotes&quot; approach over the full Numina approach), but effectively yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:59:39-07:00","id":1408587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408584#post1408584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would count as something you could roll Hypertech to understand how it works, and possibly reverse engineer if creating Fetishes is something your character can/would do.</div> </div> </div> </div>But these dogs use spirits and spiritual magic for this. I understand that they can summon weaver spirits. But this is not hypertechnology. It is possible for technomages to create a &quot;fetish&quot;. But this is something like creating a unique device or body for &quot;program&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, Hypertech isn't a power, it's a form of understanding. If a Glass Walker learns Hypertech somehow, they could likewise study technomage created Fetishes for ideas for their own Fetishes (though Garou have easier ways to study these things). </div> </div> </div>It makes sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same deal: they can make items that would you can roll Hypertech to understand the principles behind... because that's the main thing Hypertech does when you're not a mage doing Awakened magic. </div> </div> </div>WAIT! This is not science. Hypertechnology is an &quot;alternative&quot; view of conventional science. It is based on knowledge of technology. It won't help you understand the vampiric enchanted fire sword, but it will help you understand the insane quantum-etheric laser cutter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T15:02:54-07:00","id":1408590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408574#post1408574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see<br /> So Glass walkers kinda-maybe have their own hypertech in the form of techno fetishes. Does that count as hypertech?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that depends.<br /> <br /> In the most trivial sense no, because thats a thing M20 invented and werewolf exists under another scope.<br /> <br /> However if you wanted to port the thing to Mage. I think it's debatable: Do techno-fetishes created by thechnologically oriented Dreamspeaker count?. I think that fetish created with a &quot;technomantical paradigm&quot; in mind (hint: one where the tech part it's actually important) can easily count, but, say, a tv that was possessed by a spirit trough purely mistical means likely won't.<br /> Many &quot;techno-fetishes&quot; are just normal stuff that has spirits inside making it better, but I think the more esoteric procedures like, say, the Cyberwolves implant technology, could arguably enter the realm of Hypertech<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could a vampire not create Hypertech devices with thaumaturgy and a techno-centric paradigm? They too can create fetishes at least. There aren't presently mechanics for this but the magical theory suggests it could be done. </div> </div> </div>One could argue that if Hypertech it's a thing, a Vampire vamp-tek would easily count. In that case the same applies, that is: If that vamp-tek requires one to be a vampire to use (say, it's a Ritual) then merely knowing Hypertech woudln't be enough to use it, but having that knowledge *could* be a requisite to do the ritual if the vampire wishes to code it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do technocratic sorcerers get numina/can they get numina.. </div> </div> </div>Sorcery IS a form of Numina, isn't it?. So, yeah.<br /> <br /> I mean, as far as Numina even *exists* (no rules for it in M20) and there are no new &quot;static magic&quot; rules/lore indicating Sorcerers and Mage &quot;static magic users&quot; are different creatures, what techno-sorcerers do it's Numina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-16-2020, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T15:18:08-07:00","id":1408595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408587#post1408587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But these dogs use spirits and spiritual magic for this. I understand that they can summon weaver spirits. But this is not hypertechnology. It is possible for technomages to create a &quot;fetish&quot;. But this is something like creating a unique device or body for &quot;program&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, however, on the technomage's Focus, not the function of Cyberfetishes or Hypertech (and Hypertech is explicitly capable of seeing beyond this).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WAIT! This is not science. Hypertechnology is an &quot;alternative&quot; view of conventional science. It is based on knowledge of technology. It won't help you understand the vampiric enchanted fire sword, but it will help you understand the insane quantum-etheric laser cutter. </div> </div> </div>Hypertech isn't an alternative view of science. It is, as you said, based on taking technology farther with supernatural principles. The question I was addressing was not Thaumaturgy in general, but specifically the concept of Techno-thaum.<br /> <br /> Also an important line from M20 core:<br /> <br /> &quot;In game terms, this means that a successful Hypertech roll would allow a technomancer to employ a tool or Device that would not normally work for him due to its secure or unconventional design.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:29:04-07:00","id":1408609,"title":"","content":"I think this thread has devolved into everyone trying to enforce their own head-cannons as the &quot;Truth&quot;(myself included). Ironic given this is a Mage thread.<br /> <br /> I'm just gonna say, the Mage gameline contradicts itself enough that anyone's interpretation of how hypertech is suppose to work is as valid as anyone else's. If in your setting, you want hyper-tech to let people make wonders, so be it. The books aren't clear enough for a &quot;correct&quot; answer to exist.<br /> <br /> In response to the main topic, Physic 6+ is getting into supernatural levels of understanding. It' might give the person beginner's level insight into hyper systems of physics than are inaccessible in mundane reality, like the physics behind how some types of static magic work, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:57:38-07:00","id":1408771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408609#post1408609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just gonna say, the Mage gameline contradicts itself enough that anyone's interpretation of how hypertech is suppose to work is as valid as anyone else's. If in your setting, you want hyper-tech to let people make wonders, so be it. The books aren't clear enough for a &quot;correct&quot; answer to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>While everyone it's free to do what they want with *their* setting, the books are <i>cristal clear</i> about Hypertech, the Skill, not allowing to make wonders w/o magick. There are rules about how to make Wonders, these don't enable the Skill to do that.<br /> <br /> There's no real room for debate here. Go to see those BoS rules about &quot;Technocratic facilities&quot; Prometheas talks about, it doesn't ever (like, not once) mention that they can bypass the need to use <i>awakened magick</i> to create Wonders. Wonders that create Wonders and can be used by normal people don't bypass the need to use magick - they ARE magick, they would have their own Arete (unless they're single-use Gadgets) because that's how Wonders work.<br /> <br /> The reasoning its akin to say you don't need to be a Mage to create a Wonder if you have a Mage on your payroll - which it's true, but trivially so.<br /> <br /> That's as far as the RAW goes, and the rest it's just game theory: Trying to justify that everyone can do magick because everything it's magick. There only lies madness:<br /> *If everything it's magick and werenches are Wonders, why would you need Hypertech to make Wonders?, just use regular tech if it's all the same.<br /> *If wrenches *were* Wonders (but now aren't), then why conclude that the factories that create wrenches are Wonders? - couldn't they be &quot;ex-wonders&quot; now everyday tech too?. And if neither are Wonders anymore, why conclude that one could be used to create Wonders?<br /> *Where does magick end and regular stuff start? - Mage offers no solid answer. And really: do you <i>really </i>want to start asking yourself these questions if something like the much simpler RAW it's already confusing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-17-2020, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T13:17:21-07:00","id":1408778,"title":"","content":"So... A Mage could build a machine that builds a core component for hypertech (say, a powersource, a CPU, or an energy emiter) and everyone else with hypertech could design parts around that core component? <br /> Or, say, a bunch of sleepers with the hypertech knowledge could put their tech through a mage-made machine which applies the desired properties.... <br /> <br /> Can you make items that don't need quintessence or an equivelent? Could one mass-produce hypertech if a Mage had laid the machine down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T09:53:11-07:00","id":1408962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408778#post1408778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... A Mage could build a machine that builds a core component for hypertech (say, a powersource, a CPU, or an energy emiter) and everyone else with hypertech could design parts around that core component?<br /> Or, say, a bunch of sleepers with the hypertech knowledge could put their tech through a mage-made machine which applies the desired properties....<br /> <br /> Can you make items that don't need quintessence or an equivelent? Could one mass-produce hypertech if a Mage had laid the machine down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats pretty close to how I always assumed the technocracy ran in any game I've ran.<br /> <br /> I'm also going to say the technocracy in my games circumvent quintessence requirements with Forces&gt;Prime effects. Electricity is everywhere and contains a lot of energy, &quot;energy&quot; being how technocrats see quintessence in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T13:58:44-07:00","id":1409000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408778#post1408778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... A Mage could build a machine that builds a core component for hypertech (say, a powersource, a CPU, or an energy emiter) and everyone else with hypertech could design parts around that core component?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a possible approach though the specifics matter.<br /> <br /> I gave an example of a plasma rifle gunsmith with a mage built machine that makes the core &quot;plasma rifle&quot; and the gunsmith can then do all the fine tuning work and customization of individuals (like installing different targeting systems, adapting different peripherals, etc.) that would certainly follow this mold. Technically it wouldn't even be constrained to rifles as the machine isn't inherently restricted by the rules to a given weapon size and the gunsmith could build varying sized plasma guns too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, say, a bunch of sleepers with the hypertech knowledge could put their tech through a mage-made machine which applies the desired properties.... </div> </div> </div>Also possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you make items that don't need quintessence or an equivelent? Could one mass-produce hypertech if a Mage had laid the machine down? </div> </div> </div>You can't really avoid the need for Quintessence for this; esp. in the hands of unawakened helpers (they're not full Sleepers if they're doing this stuff for the most part). Create Wonder generally requires Quintessence (even if you decided it didn't, the Wonders you create wouldn't work until &quot;charged&quot; up with magical energy to function even if they just contain a small amount for no other reason). Quintessence is also the only way for a non-mage operated Wonder to lower the difficulty of the magic roll to a point where it will even reliably work (you need a good deal of successes, and get far less rolls than a full mage can do).<br /> <br /> Mass production without the involvement of mages is basically impossible. Even with mages, it will be hard to rely on a non-mage work force with Wonders to imprint effects because the failure rate is going to be pretty high for anything but very minor powers (even at the lowest possible end, the failure rate would be unacceptably high compared to any mass production line standards).<br /> <br /> There's also an issue in that the Quintessence availability in a given Mage game is a dial left to the ST to set based on the tone of the game. If dialed low, creating a Quintessence infrastructure for such an effort would be vastly more costly than the production would justify. If dialed to the max, it would be much easier to pull off so that the Technocracy has lots of non-mages armed to the teeth with medium level magical gear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1408962#post1408962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also going to say the technocracy in my games circumvent quintessence requirements with Forces&gt;Prime effects. Electricity is everywhere and contains a lot of energy, &quot;energy&quot; being how technocrats see quintessence in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>While everyone is free to do things how they want at there table, I'm going to point out this is a massive departure from the game as written on a few levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T10:21:49-07:00","id":1409169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409000#post1409000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While everyone is free to do things how they want at there table, I'm going to point out this is a massive departure from the game as written on a few levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would diminish the importance Primal Utility and the Syndicate have in the latest books, and the importance wars for nodes and other experiments to squeeze as much juice as possible had in the first books<br /> <br /> I'm not agaist ruling a way to convert electricity back into Quint, but I do think the ratio needs to be poor/costly enough as to not steal the thunder of the more typical methods. Mostly because figths for resources are fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T10:41:08-07:00","id":1409172,"title":"","content":"The RAW answer is pretty simple, as you have two choices:<br /> <br /> 1) A Node (or whatever high Prime stuff you use) is modified to create energy-tass that powers Hypertech stuff's Quintessence. Basically, you can't draw more out of energy than you put in at some other point in the line, and electricity is just delivery mechanism.<br /> <br /> 2) You have to actually destroy the Pattern you're taking Quintessence from. If you draw Quintessence straight out of electricity, you're destroying the electricity so it can't do anything else. You can't do this in parts either (just like sacrificing Life Patterns, you've got to actually sacrifice them). If you want to destroy all the electricity in your building's main circuit for a few dots of Quintessence, causing a fairly obvious localized blackout, you can do that... but there's a reason why most mages don't really like this option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T14:15:59-07:00","id":1409219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409169#post1409169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would diminish the importance Primal Utility and the Syndicate have in the latest books, and the importance wars for nodes and other experiments to squeeze as much juice as possible had in the first books<br /> <br /> I'm not agaist ruling a way to convert electricity back into Quint, but I do think the ratio needs to be poor/costly enough as to not steal the thunder of the more typical methods. Mostly because figths for resources are fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primal utility has already been diminished in M20. It can now only treat businesses that inovate new ideas on a regular basis into nodes(So, Walmat is no longer a 5+ node anymore). I'd also argue the syndicate is still important for the fact someone has to Pay that energy bill.<br /> <br /> It also lines up with real life better, tech becomes more energy hungry as it advances and one of the biggest crisis(es?) that is happening is the energy crisis. Every government and company is scrambling for a cheap and effective way to power all the new tech without choking the planet to death in a cloud of fossil fuel by-products.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue that it's in line with how the setting explained the technocracy coming into power. That while the &quot;traditional&quot; mages were squabbling over nodes and artifacts of power, the free-masons were earning the hearts and minds of the people and exploring new ways to solve quintessence problems. The fact they have Primal utility at all is an extension of that(I think, I can't pretend I know what the writers intended)<br /> <br /> It also doesn't mean that the technocrats wouldn't continuously need more and better quintessence sources to keep growing the monolith. I also run that technocratic wonders need to spend quintessence to work, so if you didn't charge your plasma pistol then it won't fire anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409172#post1409172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The RAW answer is pretty simple, as you have two choices:<br /> <br /> 1) A Node (or whatever high Prime stuff you use) is modified to create energy-tass that powers Hypertech stuff's Quintessence. Basically, you can't draw more out of energy than you put in at some other point in the line, and electricity is just delivery mechanism.<br /> <br /> 2) You have to actually destroy the Pattern you're taking Quintessence from. If you draw Quintessence straight out of electricity, you're destroying the electricity so it can't do anything else. You can't do this in parts either (just like sacrificing Life Patterns, you've got to actually sacrifice them). If you want to destroy all the electricity in your building's main circuit for a few dots of Quintessence, causing a fairly obvious localized blackout, you can do that... but there's a reason why most mages don't really like this option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how this is different from real life?<br /> <br /> If you use electricity to power something, it's spent. The concept of thermodynamic entropy IRL covers this; when energy is spent, It's gone as unrecoverable heat.<br /> <br /> You've also lost me on the &quot;not doing this in parts thing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:00:06-07:00","id":1409229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409219#post1409219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal utility has already been diminished in M20. It can now only treat businesses that inovate new ideas on a regular basis into nodes(So, Walmat is no longer a 5+ node anymore). I'd also argue the syndicate is still important for the fact someone has to Pay that energy bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book isn't nearly this restrictive with what it can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That while the &quot;traditional&quot; mages were squabbling over nodes and artifacts of power, the free-masons were earning the hearts and minds of the people and exploring new ways to solve quintessence problems. </div> </div> </div>The Order of Reason and later the Union are both described as focusing on controlling Nodes to fuel their efforts. Swaying the hearts and minds of the people eventually lead to Primal Utility, sure, but that was a ways down the line from how things started.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see how this is different from real life? </div> </div> </div>Real life doesn't have super-special magic juice that fuels everything basically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you use electricity to power something, it's spent. The concept of thermodynamic entropy IRL covers this; when energy is spent, It's gone as unrecoverable heat. </div> </div> </div>Heat isn't unrecoverable. And the difference is between transforming one form of energy into a different form of energy to perform work, and destroying one form of energy to create a better form of energy (which means it's actually the opposite of thermodynamic entropy).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You've also lost me on the &quot;not doing this in parts thing&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Patterns can't sustain themselves if you tap into them directly to draw Quintessence out of (baring mages who can refill their personal Quintessence). If you can't just plug a hypertech device into a wall socket and siphon Quintessence from the electrical current like it was a normal appliance. If you want to gain points of Quintessence it has to attack the whole Forces Pattern and destroy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T16:38:52-07:00","id":1409248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409229#post1409229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heat isn't unrecoverable. And the difference is between transforming one form of energy into a different form of energy to perform work, and destroying one form of energy to create a better form of energy (which means it's actually the opposite of thermodynamic entropy).</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of is? Any process that deals with energy produces waste heat and heat energy doesn't directly convert into usable energy percentage-wise to make up for energy lost. Unless you reverse entropy, it's pretty unrecoverable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409229#post1409229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Patterns can't sustain themselves if you tap into them directly to draw Quintessence out of (baring mages who can refill their personal Quintessence). If you can't just plug a hypertech device into a wall socket and siphon Quintessence from the electrical current like it was a normal appliance. If you want to gain points of Quintessence it has to attack the whole Forces Pattern and destroy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you can do something similar with mind patterns to convert willpower points to quintessence(though that might have been a 2nd edition thing, I don't remember).<br /> <br /> I still don't understand what you mean. Even if you &quot;destroy the forces pattern&quot;, you'd still be able to charge the plasma gun by plugging it into a wall socket. At most there just wouldn't be any electrons flowing back to the power plant or to ground, but it likely wouldn't even do that as you're converting electrical &quot;Force&quot;(volts, amps, and hertz) not &quot;Matter&quot; particles(the electrons).<br /> <br /> I apologize, but I still don't see your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T05:05:01-07:00","id":1409330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409219#post1409219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also lines up with real life better, tech becomes more energy hungry as it advances and one of the biggest crisis(es?) that is happening is the energy crisis. Every government and company is scrambling for a cheap and effective way to power all the new tech without choking the planet to death in a cloud of fossil fuel by-products.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Tech is becoming more energy effecient by and large. The problem is more people are wanting access to smartphones and personal computers, but on the flipside, less and less young people are seeing their own cars as a neccessity. Electric vehicles might use a lot of electricity, but even an EV from the worst electricity source (say, a coal fired plant) is better than the best petrol car after a relatively short period (Getting the lithium for the batteries is a big upfront cost) <br /> <br /> The issue isn't an engineering one, it's a political/business one; Engineers agree on nuclear power. More nuclear power plants would solve our energy problems and it's clean. Politically a lot of people are afraid of nuclear energy and want to look to wind and solar power... despite the problems they have (they're only active at certain times of the day, you'll need big batteries which has the lithium problem if you want to just use turbines and solar pannels...) . There's also the fact that coal businesses do not want nuclear energy to start making steam. When Germany wanted to 'go green' and shut down it's nuclear power plants, it had an energy shortage, and so opened up far-worse brown coal power plants to replace the clean nuclear ones. <br /> <br /> (storage for nuclear is an exaggerated problem, the waste product is absolutely tiny) <br /> <br /> But I suppose that's the world of darkness; &quot;It's not an engineering problem, it's a political one&quot; sums up a lot of things. We could solve world hunger too if it wasn't communism. You could point out that improving lithium batteries is an engineering problem, but it'd be less of one if <s>we just succumbed to the faint glow of Uranium</s> I mean we used nuclear power more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T07:16:37-07:00","id":1409346,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that all of that it's hard to reduce to an actual story w/o ending with Mage: The Proselitizing, the game where we talk about the normal life of normal people. A generic political agenda any person or gameline could have w/o need of actual Technocrats<br /> <br /> I dunno. At the very least, Matter to Quint conversion states that the object needs to be &quot;significant&quot; (so you can't just divide your trash into small portions to sacrifice, to have endless Quint at Prime 3). I do think that electricity to Quint conversion should also erase a &quot;significant&quot; amount/proportion. Enough to justify creating a facility that sucks the quint from prisioners or workers to power HitMarks, or defiling a Node to place your lab, rather than less unsavory methods like building some solar panels (or pay a little more for your electricity like every capitalist does).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal utility has already been diminished in M20. It can now only treat businesses that inovate new ideas on a regular basis into nodes(So, Walmat is no longer a 5+ node anymore). I'd also argue the syndicate is still important for the fact someone has to Pay that energy bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having some restrictions would be as bad as just plugging your Wonders. Syndicate: Revised (the place where it was invented, and also established as one of the main thunders of the Syndicate within the Union) placed similar restrictions (though not as bad as what you say. Wallmart itself could be a big node, but not <i>every </i>Wallmart). And I think these were good, precisely because they make more reasonable to have more unsavory methods in place like (as per the same book) exploiting workers to their deaths for Quint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-20-2020, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T13:18:26-07:00","id":1409410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409330#post1409330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tech is becoming more energy effecient by and large. The problem is more people are wanting access to smartphones and personal computers, but on the flipside, less and less young people are seeing their own cars as a neccessity. Electric vehicles might use a lot of electricity, but even an EV from the worst electricity source (say, a coal fired plant) is better than the best petrol car after a relatively short period (Getting the lithium for the batteries is a big upfront cost)<br /> <br /> The issue isn't an engineering one, it's a political/business one; Engineers agree on nuclear power. More nuclear power plants would solve our energy problems and it's clean. Politically a lot of people are afraid of nuclear energy and want to look to wind and solar power... despite the problems they have (they're only active at certain times of the day, you'll need big batteries which has the lithium problem if you want to just use turbines and solar pannels...) . There's also the fact that coal businesses do not want nuclear energy to start making steam. When Germany wanted to 'go green' and shut down it's nuclear power plants, it had an energy shortage, and so opened up far-worse brown coal power plants to replace the clean nuclear ones.<br /> <br /> (storage for nuclear is an exaggerated problem, the waste product is absolutely tiny)<br /> <br /> But I suppose that's the world of darkness; &quot;It's not an engineering problem, it's a political one&quot; sums up a lot of things. We could solve world hunger too if it wasn't communism. You could point out that improving lithium batteries is an engineering problem, but it'd be less of one if <s>we just succumbed to the faint glow of Uranium</s> I mean we used nuclear power more.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't even need uranium, molten sodium/thorium reactors are just as energetic, don't have are fuel source that's poisonous to mine, and are less likely to fail catastrophically. Unfortunately, they also can't be used to create enriched uranium/plutonium biproducts and are useless for creating nuclear weapons, so most governments aren't interested in making them.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to say that while individual components are becoming more energy efficient, complex systems like computer rigs are still becoming more energy hungry to increase processing power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409346#post1409346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that all of that it's hard to reduce to an actual story w/o ending with Mage: The Proselitizing, the game where we talk about the normal life of normal people. A generic political agenda any person or gameline could have w/o need of actual Technocrats<br /> <br /> I dunno. At the very least, Matter to Quint conversion states that the object needs to be &quot;significant&quot; (so you can't just divide your trash into small portions to sacrifice, to have endless Quint at Prime 3). I do think that electricity to Quint conversion should also erase a &quot;significant&quot; amount/proportion. Enough to justify creating a facility that sucks the quint from prisioners or workers to power HitMarks, or defiling a Node to place your lab, rather than less unsavory methods like building some solar panels (or pay a little more for your electricity like every capitalist does).<br /> <br /> Not having some restrictions would be as bad as just plugging your Wonders. Syndicate: Revised (the place where it was invented, and also established as one of the main thunders of the Syndicate within the Union) placed similar restrictions (though not as bad as what you say. Wallmart itself could be a big node, but not <i>every </i>Wallmart). And I think these were good, precisely because they make more reasonable to have more unsavory methods in place like (as per the same book) exploiting workers to their deaths for Quint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you'd define &quot;significant&quot; in this case though, especially considering how the spheres are divided. Mind, Forces, Time, or Correspondence to Prime conversions wouldn't get rid of anything physical and convert things that are, in many cases, functionally infinite.<br /> <br /> In fact, if you aren't running a &quot;consensual reality&quot; setting(in which all tech is true magic and space is an illusion painted over the spirit world) then Correspondence to Prime is an infinite resource because the universe is expanding at an ever accelerating rate thanks to the fact that space self-replicates.<br /> <br /> If we're being honest, thinking about or taking the Mage setting to it's logical conclusions causes a lot of the inherent assumptions of the setting to fall apart. I don't think there are a lot of logical reasons to why the technocracy doesn't have easy quintessence on hand(besides Maybe limitation unknowingly self imposed by their paradigm), but not having easy quintessence is necessary to the story that the setting authors want to tell.<br /> <br /> Personally I like to find my own solutions that don't involve hand-waving things or &quot;No because the ST says so&quot; rulings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T02:10:40-07:00","id":1409496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409410#post1409410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you'd define &quot;significant&quot; in this case though, especially considering how the spheres are divided.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would, like how much Quintessence is formed in a Node, be dependent on the mood the ST wants to set. But enough to be a considerable expense or be highly noticeable to Sleepers if destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind, Forces, Time, or Correspondence to Prime conversions wouldn't get rid of anything physical and convert things that are, in many cases, functionally infinite. </div> </div> </div>Mage metaphysics deals in patterns, not &quot;physical&quot; objects. A Forces pattern is a discrete thing for magic to target, even if it lacks mass. A Mind pattern is a discrete thing for magic to target, even if it lacks physicality (outside of specific Umbral Realms). Patterns aren't infinite (well, in theory, many are numerous enough that practically they are).<br /> <br /> [quote]In fact, if you aren't running a &quot;consensual reality&quot; setting(in which all tech is true magic and space is an illusion painted over the spirit world) then Correspondence to Prime is an infinite resource because the universe is expanding at an ever accelerating rate thanks to the fact that space self-replicates.[quote]<br /> <br /> Consensual reality doesn't mean all tech is true magic, or that space is an illusion.<br /> <br /> Nor does the universe expanding mean that Correspondence is an infinite Resources because space is getting large.<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem is that you keep calling these things, &quot;X to Prime conversions,&quot; when we're talking about ripping X Patterns asunder to harvest part of the Quintessence that gave them existence in the act of destruction; which isn't a perfectly efficient process. Destroying space to harvest Quintessence means shrinking how much space there is. Harvesting Quintessence from patterns using Prime magic is not some tidy little act of magic that easily produces large sums of Quintessence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we're being honest, thinking about or taking the Mage setting to it's logical conclusions causes a lot of the inherent assumptions of the setting to fall apart. </div> </div> </div>While that's invariably true about all fictional settings on some level, you're not actually taking the Mage setting to its logical conclusions because you're adding a lot of your own assumptions to the mix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think there are a lot of logical reasons to why the technocracy doesn't have easy quintessence on hand(besides Maybe limitation unknowingly self imposed by their paradigm), but not having easy quintessence is necessary to the story that the setting authors want to tell. </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy has the best access to Quintessence in the setting because they have a unique sources in the form of Primal Utility, on top of being in a position of power to have taken the most Nodes over the course of events.<br /> <br /> If you assume that a 9 volt battery can produce 1 Quintessence an hour instead of electricity (and can always be recharged), of course it seems illogical that the Technocracy doesn't have loads of Quintessence on hand.<br /> <br /> If you actually follow the logic of the setting, where you'd need to drain all the electricity out of a few million batteries in a process that would also make them basically useless as batteries again, and you might get 1-2 Quintessence for your trouble from all of it, it makes perfect sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T02:56:57-07:00","id":1409506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409496#post1409496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would, like how much Quintessence is formed in a Node, be dependent on the mood the ST wants to set. But enough to be a considerable expense or be highly noticeable to Sleepers if destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409496#post1409496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage metaphysics deals in patterns, not &quot;physical&quot; objects. A Forces pattern is a discrete thing for magic to target, even if it lacks mass. A Mind pattern is a discrete thing for magic to target, even if it lacks physicality (outside of specific Umbral Realms). Patterns aren't infinite (<b>well, in theory, many are numerous enough that practically they are</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, That was my point.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1409496]<br /> [quote]In fact, if you aren't running a &quot;consensual reality&quot; setting(in which all tech is true magic and space is an illusion painted over the spirit world) then Correspondence to Prime is an infinite resource because the universe is expanding at an ever accelerating rate thanks to the fact that space self-replicates.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Consensual reality doesn't mean all tech is true magic, or that space is an illusion. </div> </div> </div>Those are things that the old guide to the technocracy books state. If you through that out, then you're also throwing out a large portion of the setting idea that all of reality is consensual. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409496#post1409496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nor does the universe expanding mean that Correspondence is an infinite Resources because space is getting large.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not &quot;getting large&quot;, it's expanding at a rate that that accelerates as the amount of space grows. If that is a thing happening in your setting, then space is a <b>functionally</b> infinite resource thanks to the fact it can reproduce itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409496#post1409496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the problem is that you keep calling these things, &quot;X to Prime conversions,&quot; when we're talking about ripping X Patterns asunder to harvest part of the Quintessence that gave them existence in the act of destruction; which isn't a perfectly efficient process. Destroying space to harvest Quintessence means shrinking how much space there is. Harvesting Quintessence from patterns using Prime magic is not some tidy little act of magic that easily produces large sums of Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true about all reactions that produce energy. Nuclear energy is the most efficient way we've found to reliably produce, but it only converts 0.08% of the uranium's mass to energy and Then more than half the energy produced is lost when converted to electricity via turbine.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about a functionally infinite fuel source, then conversion ratio doesn't matter for the same reasons that our electricity conversions can be so terrible and still power all of human civilization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409496#post1409496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that's invariably true about all fictional settings on some level, you're not actually taking the Mage setting to its logical conclusions because you're adding a lot of your own assumptions to the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I don't think anyone in this comment section or even anyone who plays mage is guiltless of that. Mage is self-contradictory at the best of times and everyone have their own &quot;Paradigm&quot; when running it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409496#post1409496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy has the best access to Quintessence in the setting because they have a unique sources in the form of Primal Utility, on top of being in a position of power to have taken the most Nodes over the course of events.<br /> <br /> If you assume that a 9 volt battery can produce 1 Quintessence an hour instead of electricity (and can always be recharged), of course it seems illogical that the Technocracy doesn't have loads of Quintessence on hand.<br /> <br /> If you actually follow the logic of the setting, where you'd need to drain all the electricity out of a few million batteries in a process that would also make them basically useless as batteries again, and you might get 1-2 Quintessence for your trouble from all of it, it makes perfect sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking that needing millions of batteries to get 2 quintessence is stretching the &quot;noticeable to sleepers&quot; line a bit. On the other hand, that's 18 hours on a power line so it just makes 9V batteries inefficient for quintessence.<br /> <br /> The &quot;useless as batteries&quot; part seems unnecessary, most things are useless after you drain them directly of energy(gas, non-rechargable batteries, enriched uranium), but things that aren't also don't happen to be the thing you're draining(rechargable batteries and power lines aren't the things producing electricity, they just hold it).<br /> <br /> If you're trying to tell be that the power lines in the earlier example would become useless, then I'm going to stop you there. The power lines aren't the pattern being tapped, the electricity is. Trying to say that is like saying that pattern tapping water in a river would destroy the earth because the river was running on soil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T07:25:53-07:00","id":1409555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409506#post1409506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true about all reactions that produce energy. Nuclear energy is the most efficient way we've found to reliably produce, but it only converts 0.08% of the uranium's mass to energy and Then more than half the energy produced is lost when converted to electricity via turbine.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about a functionally infinite fuel source, then conversion ratio doesn't matter for the same reasons that our electricity conversions can be so terrible and still power all of human civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can matter a lot, because resources still need to be grasped. It makes the endeavor Vulgar if you're taking so much it's noticeable. It makes it functionally impossible if the action it's so monumental it ends becoming a godlike feat+ . It may make it a bad idea altogether if it just makes it more difficult than the alternatives.<br /> <br /> An absurd example: If converting local space into energy to ligth a bulb causes catastrophical fluctuatios trough the whole planetary system as the planet's orbit shrink so much they start coliding with the sun, you would want to take your &quot;space&quot; very, very far away - and when you could always connect that bulb to a potato to ligth it, it's taking space really a good idea?<br /> <br /> More so, almost everything in the universe it's <b>functionally </b>infinite for our purposes. Matter it's also functionally infinite: With the amount of planets and other celestial bodies there's out there you will never realistically exhaust it. Everything in the universe it's functionally infinite from the perspective of motes of cosmic dust like us, except perhaps life. The problem it's to be able to take it - and the conversion ratio matters because of that, you don't have access to the whole of the universe at the same time: you have to set your workshop somewhere and make it work. And that's where complications migth arise.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not convinced you can transform space into Quintessence. You need Corr 5 at least to &quot;create&quot; (enlarge) space, and it doesn't cost Quint (doesn't it?) - why should it give Quint back to &quot;erase&quot; it?. But that's besides the point. It doesn't matter if your resource it's &quot;functionally infinite&quot; in the universe if harvesting it is inconvenient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that needing millions of batteries to get 2 quintessence is stretching the &quot;noticeable to sleepers&quot; line a bit. On the other hand, that's 18 hours on a power line so it just makes 9V batteries inefficient for quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's only if you measure the conversion cuantitatively (and the game says that's not the case, as it's not the amount of Matter what it matters as per the few vague indications we have). Which get's us to your doubt:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you'd define &quot;significant&quot; in this case though<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Personally I like to find my own solutions that don't involve hand-waving things or &quot;No because the ST says so&quot; rulings.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no rules to convert Forces into Quintessence, it's just vaguely implied that you should be able to do it. Hence you're necessarily on &quot;ST says so&quot; territory here.<br /> <br /> Now we're trying to think why the Technocracy canonically does other (seemingly much more inconvinient) stuff, when this it's possible. Otherwise you'e handwaving the setting, like a lot. The reasonable answer here, that doesn't involve a lot of of that hand-wave you don't like, it's &quot;because plugging your stuff it's not that convinient for some reason&quot;<br /> <br /> So, I define significant as &quot;significant&quot;. As in: It has to be a hassle, otherwise you're sacrificing countless chapters of the Mage setting for a single line of fluff inside a Sphere. I would recommend not to take a cuantitative approach (that the book already kills in the one place you can grab to even think the conversion should be possible in the first place) because to make it a hassle for the Technos you would have to put such a ludicrously large number than nobody else would ever be able to do it,<br /> <br /> It's an interesting solution to say that in order for the conversion to work it has to take the pattern &quot;out of work&quot; for a while, as Heavy Arms stated: Lemme explain how that could work:<br /> <br /> The idea it's that the energy inside the power grid it's a flow as far as Forces are concerned, but it's a single form as far as Prime it's concerned. It's like you're damaging the idea of &quot;having ligth&quot; rather than just moving or transforming the energy. This does jive with the way Prime 2 creates stuff (as platonic objects), and thus it's at least every bit as canon as the vague concept of turning Forces back into Prime (that's an extrapolation of what you can do to Matter, that also hasn't clear rules).<br /> If it's bizarre that the socket where you connected your rifle won't work anymore for a day or two ('til the Pattern regens) in spire of the fact the cables are allrigth and working (the energy just doesn't seem to go in for some reason lower-case science can't explain, but enlightened science can) then that just means the conversion it's Vulgar, also a danger to the &quot;Masquerade&quot;...and all the more reason for the Technocracy (and other people) to rather use other, less savory or seemingly less convinient, means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-21-2020, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T13:34:01-07:00","id":1409617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409555#post1409555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...There's no rules to convert Forces into Quintessence, it's just vaguely implied that you should be able to do it. Hence you're necessarily on &quot;ST says so&quot; territory here.<br /> <br /> Now we're trying to think why the Technocracy canonically does other (seemingly much more inconvinient) stuff, when this it's possible. Otherwise you'e handwaving the setting, like a lot. The reasonable answer here, that doesn't involve a lot of of that hand-wave you don't like, it's &quot;because plugging your stuff it's not that convinient for some reason&quot;<br /> <br /> So, I define significant as &quot;significant&quot;. As in: It has to be a hassle, otherwise you're sacrificing countless chapters of the Mage setting for a single line of fluff inside a Sphere. I would recommend not to take a cuantitative approach (that the book already kills in the one place you can grab to even think the conversion should be possible in the first place) because to make it a hassle for the Technos you would have to put such a ludicrously large number than nobody else would ever be able to do it,<br /> <br /> It's an interesting solution to say that in order for the conversion to work it has to take the pattern &quot;out of work&quot; for a while, as Heavy Arms stated: Lemme explain how that could work:<br /> <br /> The idea it's that the energy inside the power grid it's a flow as far as Forces are concerned, but it's a single form as far as Prime it's concerned. It's like you're damaging the idea of &quot;having ligth&quot; rather than just moving or transforming the energy. This does jive with the way Prime 2 creates stuff (as platonic objects), and thus it's at least every bit as canon as the vague concept of turning Forces back into Prime (that's an extrapolation of what you can do to Matter, that also hasn't clear rules).<br /> If it's bizarre that the socket where you connected your rifle won't work anymore for a day or two ('til the Pattern regens) in spire of the fact the cables are allrigth and working (the energy just doesn't seem to go in for some reason lower-case science can't explain, but enlightened science can) then that just means the conversion it's Vulgar, also a danger to the &quot;Masquerade&quot;...and all the more reason for the Technocracy (and other people) to rather use other, less savory or seemingly less convinient, means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I think I can see the root of the argument here and I think it comes down to ST styles.<br /> <br /> The direction you seem to be coming from is(if I'm understanding correctly): [Sees area rules don't necessarily cover]&gt;[considers setting]&gt;[creates rules for session based on what makes sense for existing setting].<br /> <br /> My thought process in contrast follows: [Sees area rules don't necessarily cover]&gt;[considers closest real life example]&gt;[creates rules based on IRL example]&gt;[Sees rules cause conflict with established setting]&gt;[changes setting]<br /> <br /> The pattern ubiquity thing rubs me the wrong way because I compare to IRL while you are coming from the stance of preserving the Mage Setting itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T13:47:47-07:00","id":1409621,"title":"","content":"Batterys degrade and you need specific fluids to get around that: Beyond eletrical power there is usually some believable (at least you believe it) rationale as to why simple solutions don't work. And if electrical grids worked for the technocracy, one must wonder why tradition mages arent supercharged by more geography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T14:04:17-07:00","id":1409624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409617#post1409617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thought process in contrast follows: [Sees area rules don't necessarily cover]&gt;[considers closest real life example]&gt;[creates rules based on IRL example]&gt;[Sees rules cause conflict with established setting]&gt;[changes setting]<br /> <br /> The pattern ubiquity thing rubs me the wrong way because I compare to IRL while you are coming from the stance of preserving the Mage Setting itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is why your talk of &quot;taking the setting to it's logical conclusion&quot; doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Magic explicitly <b>does not</b> follow the rules of real life. That's what makes it magic. If you use the &quot;closest real life example&quot; without any look at the closest canon magical example, you're not talking about the game or its setting any more, you're talking about your house rules causing contradictions that aren't in the original text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T17:12:49-07:00","id":1409653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409621#post1409621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batterys degrade and you need specific fluids to get around that: Beyond eletrical power there is usually some believable (at least you believe it) rationale as to why simple solutions don't work. And if electrical grids worked for the technocracy, one must wonder why tradition mages arent supercharged by more geography.</div> </div> </div> </div>Battery degradation is definitely a thing, but I think mage has that covered by paradox rules.<br /> <br /> As for tradition mages getting supercharged by geography, they could. Why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409624#post1409624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is why your talk of &quot;taking the setting to it's logical conclusion&quot; doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Magic explicitly <b>does not</b> follow the rules of real life. That's what makes it magic. If you use the &quot;closest real life example&quot; without any look at the closest canon magical example, you're not talking about the game or its setting any more, you're talking about your house rules causing contradictions that aren't in the original text.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Any sufficiently understood magic system becomes another field of science&quot;. Alchemy was magic until it became chemistry.<br /> <br /> By &quot;Logical Conclusion&quot; I pretty much mean &quot;what is a real world modern scientist going to try to do if they have access to Mage's magic system&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of those things would definitely be to try to find a good fuel source to convert to quintessence for en easy supply. Pattern shredding for quintessence is supported by rules(even if they're vague) and many of the patterns available to mages are &quot;functionally&quot; infinite or fast-replenishing while also being ethereal enough that they don't effect physical reality in a meaningful way when destroyed. Even at terrible conversion ratios, the technocracy having massive to infinite amounts of quintessence is the only conclusion I can come to without creating house-rules specifically to preserve the setting. <br /> <br /> World of Darkness, like most RPGs, has &quot;things function as in real life when exceptions aren't explicitly stated&quot; written into it's setting so that authors don't have to explain the entirety of the universe's physics. That comes with the inherent &quot;stranger than fiction&quot; baggage that Real Life has. Mage's setting, like a lot of RPGs and most sci-fi, has a lot of assumptions inherent to it that fall apart when you compare them to similar situations in reality. That's fine, but I like using real life to inspire plots for my sessions.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way, IRL humans exist in a universe that only has the minimum physics required for them to exist in the first place. No special powers, no obvious signs of external help. Yet look at how much humanity has &quot;gamed the system&quot; and broken any semblance of &quot;balance&quot; our reality had. There's a channel on youtube called &quot;Tierzoo&quot; that talks about evolution like a video game(and it's surprisingly balanced) that highlights this sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T20:20:36-07:00","id":1409689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409653#post1409653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Any sufficiently understood magic system becomes another field of science&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting quotes around words doesn't make them true even if someone somewhere might have actually uttered those words in that order.<br /> <br /> Clarke's third law goes in the other direction, not in both directions. Clarke's laws are also about writing science fiction, not a factual statement about reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alchemy was magic until it became chemistry. </div> </div> </div>Chemistry didn't poof into existence after alchemy was around for awhile. This is entirely reductionist, historical revisionist, and Eurocentric beyond being any form of useful as a statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By &quot;Logical Conclusion&quot; I pretty much mean &quot;what is a real world modern scientist going to try to do if they have access to Mage's magic system&quot;. </div> </div> </div>So... you're just goal post shifting because the idea that you meant that in the first place is completely illogical?<br /> <br /> Also, what a real world modern scientist would try to do is meaningless. What the results would be? That matters. And that's how you get the Society of Ether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of those things would definitely be to try to find a good fuel source to convert to quintessence for en easy supply. </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, that doesn't exist, because Quintessence follows mystic laws like the law of sympathy (which is actually why Primal Utility makes sense!) where subjective value is more important than some sort of objective energetic state. What would seem a paradox to a modern scientist, anything that makes something a good fuel sources for Quintessence inherently makes it a bad fuel source, because Quintessence is defined by it's rarity and difficulty to mass produce.<br /> <br /> Changing the setting to make such a fuel exist is your own problem for other parts of the setting not playing well with the change. Just because mages might want it to exist doesn't mean they can actually make it happen. Mages want lots of things that it turns out don't just happen even with lots of magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pattern shredding for quintessence is supported by rules(even if they're vague) and many of the patterns available to mages are &quot;functionally&quot; infinite or fast-replenishing while also being ethereal enough that they don't effect physical reality in a meaningful way when destroyed. </div> </div> </div>There's enough wood on Earth that no individual can burn enough for fuel to have any significant impact on the environment. That ceases to be true with lots of people doing it.<br /> <br /> The same applies to mages. Just because one mage can't shred enough Patterns of the right kinds to seriously damage anything doesn't mean that organizations like the Technocracy can do so without causing massive disruption to the universe. Also the &quot;ethereal&quot; Patterns can't be harmed without an impact on the physical Realm. If you feed dreams and ideas into your Mind harvesting machine en mass, you start doing serious damage to human psyches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even at terrible conversion ratios, the technocracy having massive to infinite amounts of quintessence is the only conclusion I can come to without creating house-rules specifically to preserve the setting. </div> </div> </div>You're completely skipping how much over time. Infinite Quintessence over infinite time is simple. It doesn't mean they'll have infinite access all the time.<br /> <br /> And of course, all the other things we keep bringing up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> World of Darkness, like most RPGs, has &quot;things function as in real life when exceptions aren't explicitly stated&quot; written into it's setting so that authors don't have to explain the entirety of the universe's physics. </div> </div> </div>And we're in the &quot;explicitly stated as not working like real life,&quot; part of the setting so... yeah.<br /> <br /> [quote]Mage's setting, like a lot of RPGs and most sci-fi, has a lot of assumptions inherent to it that fall apart when you compare them to similar situations in reality. That's fine, but I like using real life to inspire plots for my sessions.[/quote<br /> <br /> There's plenty of ways to use real life to inspire plots without changing the setting for the sole purpose of breaking it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think of it this way, IRL humans exist in a universe that only has the minimum physics required for them to exist in the first place. </div> </div> </div>This is not true. We have no idea where in the conceptual range of &quot;minimum&quot; physics to &quot;maximum physics&quot; required for humanity to exist things actually are, because the universe does not exist just to form humans. As a matter of tautology the universe we live in has to be one that supports human life, because we exist in it. That doesn't mean there's any evidence that the universe only has the minimum physics required for humans to exist because there's no evidence that the universe exists just to make use. Since we have lots of evidence to show we are not the destiny of the universe purely based on the laws of physics, there has to be the minimum for everything else we know can and could exist too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yet look at how much humanity has &quot;gamed the system&quot; and broken any semblance of &quot;balance&quot; our reality had. </div> </div> </div>We haven't gamed the system in any particularly special way, nor does reality have any semblance of balance to have broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a channel on youtube called &quot;Tierzoo&quot; that talks about evolution like a video game(and it's surprisingly balanced) that highlights this sometimes. </div> </div> </div>It's great for being a neat framing device, but highly biasing in presenting things as being done purposefully. There isn't an intelligence behind evolution deciding things are OP, or that something it getting nerfed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T02:36:23-07:00","id":1409725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409689#post1409689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus christ dude, calm down. I'm not trying to insult the game or way you play it. I'm not angrily ranting on the internet. If you feel I've written a post to insult you then I apologize, but that is not my intention.<br /> <br /> That is an actual quote though, and it applies to literature. The more a reader knows about a magic system, the less &quot;Magical&quot; it becomes and more it becomes like a nifty set of super-powers. That's especially true if the characters are able to use them often and reliably. This also comes into conflict with &quot;A magic system can only be as useful as the readers understanding of it&quot;, which I probably messed up but it essentially boils down to the fact that your readers need to know the applications and limits of any magic system for it not to seem like a convenient Deus ex Machina to the reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T06:18:51-07:00","id":1409752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409725#post1409725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus christ dude, calm down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything I posted in that &quot;snip&quot; was perfectly calmly written. Maybe don't project so much? I didn't accuse your of insulting anyone or angrily ranting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you feel I've written a post to insult you then I apologize, but that is not my intention. </div> </div> </div>Well, this actually pisses me off, because non-apologies are annoying.<br /> <br /> The implication here is frustratingly clear: Instead of actually wanting to engage with the discussion, since it wasn't really going well for your position, you've purposefully mischaracterized my post as some sort of angry screed, fake apologized for causing a non-existent outburst which is thus meaningless, and thoroughly distracted from everything I actually said.<br /> <br /> If you feel like apologizing for that? I'm willing to see what you have to say.<br /> <br /> I know I'm a notoriously easy to provoke poster, but it takes a lot more than this boring rhetorical slop to actually get me to blow my stack... and it's a hell of a lot more obvious when I do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is an actual quote though, and it applies to literature. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't actually dispute my response to it, esp. the part where you directly linked it to the real world exchange of ideas between alchemy and chemistry and didn't just keep it as a point about literature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The more a reader knows about a magic system, the less &quot;Magical&quot; it becomes and more it becomes like a nifty set of super-powers. </div> </div> </div>And yet you're the one arguing to make Mage less magical in all this by arguing to remove aspects of the setting that are clearly understood (why Quintessence harvesting is inherently paradoxical, no mage in the setting can actually tell you why even if some have good guesses), and even highlighted that your way of interpreting and changing the setting is one that emphasizes explaining more to the readers instead of leaving more unexplained (such as the whole wanting to avoid ST handwaving).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's especially true if the characters are able to use them often and reliably. </div> </div> </div>And while most experienced mage players have long since learned how to game its mechanics all too well, the intention of the game and setting is that magic isn't reliable. Even the Technocracy is constantly pictured as being frustrated that no matter how well they do their theories, quadruple check their math, and all of their process... they have constant setbacks as magic just doesn't bend the way they want it to bend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also comes into conflict with &quot;A magic system can only be as useful as the readers understanding of it&quot;, which I probably messed up but it essentially boils down to the fact that your readers need to know the applications and limits of any magic system for it not to seem like a convenient Deus ex Machina to the reader. </div> </div> </div>I think you're severely misunderstanding Sanderson here (the quote being, &quot;An author's ability to solve conflict with magic is directly proportional to how well the reader understands said magic.&quot;)<br /> <br /> It only comes into &quot;conflict&quot; in as much as Sanderson rejects the idea completely that hard magic settings are inherently &quot;unmagical&quot; just because they explain a lot to the audience. Settings that don't feel magical stem - in his model of things - from a failure to understand where on the spectrum of soft-to-hard magic a setting is, and then not applying the proper techniques to account for that creative choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T12:55:11-07:00","id":1409803,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to note that both Ehterites and the Technocracy understand that what they're doing isn't exactly science. How you say?, well, both of them have a fancy way of naming what they do: Science! v.s enlightened science - in both cases they use a terminology that sepparates what they do from what sleepers do (neither call what they do: science), in a way admiting it's not the same.<br /> <br /> I think this is very reasonable: Scientists! and scientists opperate on different &quot;layers&quot; of reality. Mundane people create and invent new tech by understanding the laws of nature and trying to bend them. So do Scientists!, but they opperate on <i>different laws</i>.<br /> Normal scietists opperate on the natural laws that are presented to them by the reality that's accepted by the Consensus, whereas Scientists! know that there are <i>deeper</i> laws (reality vs Reality) - the existence of magick (and the supernatural world) proves them rigth, even if their theories aren't necessarily rigth or sane.<br /> <br /> And that's why I cherish those moments where magick works in ways (perhaps paradoxical) that would not just be a novelty, but actually aberrant to a normal scientist (but maybe not to a &quot;crazy&quot; one, if you get what I mean). It makes the whole world more magical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-22-2020, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T13:31:46-07:00","id":1409810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409752#post1409752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything I posted in that &quot;snip&quot; was perfectly calmly written. Maybe don't project so much? I didn't accuse your of insulting anyone or angrily ranting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, this actually pisses me off, because non-apologies are annoying.<br /> <br /> The implication here is frustratingly clear: Instead of actually wanting to engage with the discussion, since it wasn't really going well for your position, you've purposefully mischaracterized my post as some sort of angry screed, fake apologized for causing a non-existent outburst which is thus meaningless, and thoroughly distracted from everything I actually said.<br /> <br /> If you feel like apologizing for that? I'm willing to see what you have to say.<br /> <br /> I know I'm a notoriously easy to provoke poster, but it takes a lot more than this boring rhetorical slop to actually get me to blow my stack... and it's a hell of a lot more obvious when I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I am angry at this. I'm not trying to argue with you that the mage setting happens to be a certain way. All of my posts have been me explaining a thing I do for my games specifically and my thought process behind why. I'm not trying to argue that the way I play my game is better than yours.<br /> <br /> From my perspective, I've spent the last page trying to argue against the insinuation that I'm having fun &quot;wrong&quot; in some way.<br /> <br /> At the start of this tangential argument, I was providing an example of something I do in games that I run to answer a question. I'm not trying to say every has to run their game the way I play, but I've felt the entire argument since has been that I shouldn't run my game that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409752#post1409752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't actually dispute my response to it, esp. the part where you directly linked it to the real world exchange of ideas between alchemy and chemistry and didn't just keep it as a point about literature...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not changing my argument(I think, not intentionally anyway). I'm providing a little factoid I thought was cool, same with the youtube channel. I tried working presenting those factoids into my argument because I liked talking about them and I guess I failed Spectacularly at making it coherent.<br /> <br /> For the related things in the last post: I didn't mean &quot;minimum physics&quot; to mean that the universe was created with us in mind. However, a lot of physicists agree that even the slightest change in the universal constants in physics would have prevented humans from evolving at all. Granted another form of intelligent &quot;being&quot; might have, but they wouldn't be Humans.<br /> <br /> I also know that real life doesn't have any form of directed &quot;Game balance&quot; as it's random, but it has a kind of balance between mutation complexity vs required calorie intake and living things filling symbiotic niches in ecosystems that can be portrayed a lot Like game balance(that's what Tierzoo does). <br /> <br /> My point with the first quote was that any &quot;Magic&quot; that people understand well enough will become mundane and exploited in safe, repeatable ways like chemistry. If my alchemy&gt;chemistry example seems reductionist to you, then fine, sure. I still stand by my original point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409752#post1409752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you're the one arguing to make Mage less magical in all this by arguing to remove aspects of the setting that are clearly understood (why Quintessence harvesting is inherently paradoxical, no mage in the setting can actually tell you why even if some have good guesses), and even highlighted that your way of interpreting and changing the setting is one that emphasizes explaining more to the readers instead of leaving more unexplained (such as the whole wanting to avoid ST handwaving).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, from the beginning, been talking about how I have fun running my games specifically and presenting why to combat the notion that I'm running the game &quot;Wrong&quot; in some way as that was what I was getting from your posts.<br /> <br /> I am not telling you how to play your game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409752#post1409752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while most experienced mage players have long since learned how to game its mechanics all too well, the intention of the game and setting is that magic isn't reliable. Even the Technocracy is constantly pictured as being frustrated that no matter how well they do their theories, quadruple check their math, and all of their process... they have constant setbacks as magic just doesn't bend the way they want it to bend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but I would like to present that rotes are a thing in setting. Magic effects that are repeatable and have worked the same way since they were first invented however long ago. You don't need All magic to be predictable for science(or Science!, or enlightened science) to happen and use that as a building off point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409752#post1409752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're severely misunderstanding Sanderson here (the quote being, &quot;An author's ability to solve conflict with magic is directly proportional to how well the reader understands said magic.&quot;)<br /> <br /> It only comes into &quot;conflict&quot; in as much as Sanderson rejects the idea completely that hard magic settings are inherently &quot;unmagical&quot; just because they explain a lot to the audience. Settings that don't feel magical stem - in his model of things - from a failure to understand where on the spectrum of soft-to-hard magic a setting is, and then not applying the proper techniques to account for that creative choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I mis-quoted and mis-understood that one. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T15:18:44-07:00","id":1409824,"title":"","content":"Friends. This is not a discussion of how magic work. This discussion was &quot;slightly&quot; different when I created it and I definitely haven't changed this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T16:26:05-07:00","id":1409828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1408190-quastions-about-inhuman-knowledge-traits-6-and-hypertech?p=1409824#post1409824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Friends. This is not a discussion of how magic work. This discussion was &quot;slightly&quot; different when I created it and I definitely haven't changed this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry. Consensus though seems to be that the vampire and werewolf could created their own versions of hypertech by substituting their own brands of magic. The scientists would likely be out of luck if they didn't get magical assistance or find some mundane work-around somehow(If that is even possible).<br /> <br /> For some references, book of the weaver is a great resource for looking at some of the flavors of magi-tech. It has examples from both technocratic devices and techno-fetishes. Anarch Blood magic also contains some nifty techno-rituals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T03:44:56-07:00","id":1409871,"title":"","content":"A knowledge rating of 6+ isn't necessarily 'you know things people do not' you haven't worked out Faster Than Light Travel or anything like that just because you have physics 8. But your <i>understanding</i> of physics is greater; You can look at someone else's paper and after a single quick reading it's as if you did all the research yourself. You're more likely to work out FTL than someone else, but the rating doesn't grant you that knowledge automatically. An engineering (aeronautica) skill of 8 doesn't mean you're creating those FTL drives, but it does mean you could probably design the F-35 with a 20 minute sketch if you paired this knowledge with good intellegence because you already know what works and what doesn't work in context with whatever., and you could probably design something better when material science or AI catches up or a scientist introduces something new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}